From: Ryan Walklin <ryan@testtoast.com>
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: add display SoC nodes and PWM
Upstream-Status: Submitted <https://lore.kernel.org/linux-arm-kernel/20250216092827.15444-1-ryan@testtoast.com/> (patches 2/8, 5/8, 6/8; adapted, see below)
Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Ryan Walklin <ryan@testtoast.com>

Add the H616/H700 display pipeline SoC nodes: display engine, DE33
bus + clocks + mixer0, TCON TOP / TCON LCD0 / TCON TV0, LCD/LVDS/PWM
pinctrl, and the PWM block. All consumables stay status="disabled";
boards enable exactly what they wire up.

Squeezebox OOT adaptations of the lore series to linux v7.3.4 (WP3):
- bus allwinner,sram points at the existing &sram_c node (v7.3.4
  already carries sram_c with the a64-sram-c fallback; the series'
  extra de3_sram section would collide with it).
- tcon_lcd0 carries only the "lcd" reset (the only reset the TCON
  driver consumes; LVDS is unused by RGB panels). Addresses Jernej's
  review on the series' LCD1-as-LVDS reset.
- tcon_top uses #clock-cells = <1> (onecell provider, as on H6) so
  the tcon_tv0 CLK_TCON_TOP_TV0 consumer resolves; drops the v1
  clock-output-names.
- adds the pwm@300a000 node (H616 PWM == H6 IP; driver match from
  patch 3/5) for pwm-backlight brightness control.

Validated: sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-h.dtb builds clean via the
kernel dtbs target; no other DTB in the tree regresses (see
docs/test-results/wp3-panel.md). Display output still HW-gated.

